Stores individual fixed assets (PPE) with their acquisition value, depreciation rules, book value, and full lifecycle accounting from purchase to disposal.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Register assets directly or from vendor bills/invoice lines
Compute and post automatic depreciation entries (linear, degressive, etc.)
Track current book value, accumulated depreciation, and residual value
Handle asset sale, scrap, partial disposal, or revaluation
Generate asset registers, depreciation forecasts, and fiscal reports
Support multi-company, multi-currency, and localization-specific rules

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent + mail.thread + activity.mixin)
Key Fields:
name (char, required), code (char, sequenced)
original_value (monetary, required), acquisition_date, disposal_date
method (selection: linear/degressive), method_number (useful life), method_period, prorata
account_asset_id, account_depreciation_id, account_depreciation_expense_id (→ account.account)
journal_id (→ account.journal)
Computed: book_value, depreciated_value, remaining_value
One2many: depreciation_move_ids / move_ids (links to posted depreciation journal entries)

Critical Hooks: action_validate, compute_depreciation_board, _post_depreciation_moves, button_dispose, onchange_original_value
Security: account.group_account_manager + company rules
Workflow: state machine (draft → open → close), cron-driven depreciation, server actions

RAG Routing Keywords:
fixed asset, PPE, asset register, depreciation board, accumulated depreciation, book value, asset disposal, asset acquisition, depreciation expense, asset lifecycle, asset code, depreciation schedule, capital asset, fixed asset accounting, draft asset, running asset, fully depreciated, disposed asset, closed asset, asset state
Related Models (most joined):

account.account (asset / depreciation / expense accounts)
account.journal (depreciation journal)
account.move & account.move.line (acquisition + depreciation postings)
account.asset.model (template, when used)
res.company

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
account.asset is the central Odoo model for fixed assets storing original_value, acquisition_date, depreciation method (linear/degressive), useful life, linked accounts (asset/depreciation/expense), journal, and computed book_value. It drives automatic creation and posting of depreciation journal entries, asset disposal, revaluation, and full integration with the general ledger via account.move. Core to the accounting assets module, heavily referenced by invoices, journals, and financial reports.